		<div class="post" id="post-2533794">
		<div class="long">
			<div class="head">
									<div class="options">
						<a href="javascript:;" onclick="togglePostFold(event,2533794)" class="btn btn-default btn-small btn-sm">Fold</a>
					</div>
								<div class="title" id="post-title-2533794">
																		
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kalinin" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2203795); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2203795&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608282638" alt="Kalinin" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2203795)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kalinin" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2203795); return false;" >Kalinin</a></span> <span class="odate time_1467869462 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">07 Jul 2016 05:31</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2533794">
									

<p>Business first. I'm not seeing what the connection is to the SCP universe, so I'm a little confused as to how this relates in any way. I'm likely missing some sort of reference to a skip I haven't read in a while, but if there is some relation, it's eluding me. There was also a few bits of the structure that didn't sit right with me; the backstory between Plagum and Glibo being sort of shoehorned in during the encounter with another character seemed a little clunky, and the ending was really abrupt. Little bits like that interfered with the flow of the story more than I would have liked.</p>
<p>That said, this was nicely immersive, and you managed to construct a world I found interesting despite my personal distaste for the whimsical in a short amount of time. That's efficient storytelling, which to me is solid writing. It also managed to avoid feeling derivative of other fantasy works, which in a story about tinkerer gnomes is quite something. I can't say that this is my sort of thing, but the writing is such that I was surprisingly engrossed. Solid work.</p>

							</div>

								
					
